## Where a TV Screen Fits: Lobbies, Exhibition Booths, Gala Dinners and Hybrid Meetings

A TV screen earns its place in scenarios a projector was never built for, because it lights itself rather than depending on a beam and a dark surface to read:

-   **Lobby and reception signage**: a welcome message, an agenda or a sponsor's logo looping in a hotel lobby or entrance, fully legible under normal daytime lighting.

-   **Exhibition booth branding**: a stand that needs to stay bright and readable on a busy exhibition floor, where dimming the area around a projector screen is not an option.

-   **Gala dinner table side displays**: a single screen positioned near the top table or stage for a slideshow, scoreboard or awards graphic during an awards format dinner.

-   **Hybrid meeting and video conferencing screens**: the MICE Pack's own purpose is corporate and meeting use, with the screen carrying the video call while the gooseneck and wireless microphones carry the room's voice back to the remote side.

None of these need a darkened room. That is the real dividing line between a TV screen and a projector: a projector's image depends on lumens fighting the room's own light, while a flat panel screen is self lit and reads the same in a bright lobby as it does in a shaded conference room.

## Is a TV Screen the Same as a Display Monitor or Plasma Screen?

Yes. Across the Malaga and Costa del Sol AV market, "TV screen," "display monitor" and "plasma screen" describe the same flat panel product, not three different ones. "Plasma screen" survives in local search as a legacy umbrella term from an older display technology that is no longer actually installed anywhere, a real pattern visible on competitor sites that still title a page "alquiler de pantallas de plasma" while listing modern LED and LCD panels underneath it. "Display monitor" is simply another name for the same flat panel screen.

Whichever of those three terms brought you here, the real product behind it at Malaga Event Gear is the same one: the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s premium 60 inch high definition LED display screen with a designer stand.

## What We Don't Stock: LED Video Walls and Modular LED Panels

There is no LED video wall or modular LED panel system in our own inventory. Our large format display is a single 60 inch flat panel screen on a designer stand, not a modular tiled video wall built from stacked LED cabinets with a published pixel pitch, brightness rating or IP rating for outdoor use.

If your event genuinely needs an LED wall or video wall, an outdoor stage scale backdrop, or a modular display sized to a specific pixel pitch, it would have to come from outside our own inventory. We do not publish pixel pitch, brightness or IP rating specs for equipment we don't own, and we won't invent a model or a price for one. Tell us the size and setting you have in mind, and we can check with our suppliers whether one of them could provide it, if any can. From our own stock, the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s 60 inch screen covers the lobby, exhibition, gala dinner and hybrid meeting use cases above.

## TV Screen or Projector: Which One Does Your Event Need?

If your room is large, needs to stay darkened, or the image needs to scale to a genuinely large screen size, a projector is the right tool: our [projector rental](/blog/projector-rental/) guide covers our 3000 lumen tier bundled with a 2x2m screen on the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), and our 5000 lumen tier bundled with a stable stand screen on the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), for rooms that stay lit during a dealership showcase or a press event.

If a single readable panel is enough, the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s TV screen is the simpler fit: nothing to focus or align, full brightness the moment it powers on, and it reads the same in a bright lobby, an exhibition hall or a gala dinner room.

