## Indoor Venues and How Far in Advance to Book

We do not publish an outdoor rating for this screen, so the honest guidance is indoor venues: conference rooms, hotel ballrooms and exhibition halls, the settings the MICE Pack is actually built for. [Contact us](/contact/) with your specific venue if you are considering an outdoor placement, and we will confirm what is possible rather than guess.

Book as early as you can once your event date is confirmed. Demand on the Costa del Sol peaks during wedding season, from April through October, for gala dinners and celebrations, and corporate bookings tied to a fixed conference or product launch date should lock in the package early rather than wait for a final headcount.

## Conclusion

A TV screen rental is the right call whenever a projector's darkened room and lumens tier are not what your event needs: a lobby, an exhibition stand, a gala dinner table or a hybrid meeting screen that has to stay legible under normal light. Malaga Event Gear delivers, installs, tests and collects the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s 60 inch high definition LED display so you never have to. [Contact us](/contact/) to match a package to your event. For our full audio visual rental range, see the [audio visual rental page](/blog/audio-visual-rental/).

## FAQs

### What screen sizes are available?

One real size: a 60 inch high definition LED display screen, included on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/). We do not publish a smaller a la carte TV screen size, and the 60 inch panel is the size in our own inventory, so it is the number to plan around. If your event needs another size or several screens, tell us, and we will see what we can put together before you commit to a layout. If your event needs a larger image, a projected one is the usual route. The screen included in our [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) is 2x2 m, and our [projector rental](/blog/projector-rental/) guide covers what to do if your room needs more than that.

### Do you rent a 55 inch screen?

Not as such, and the honest answer is that you probably do not need one. The panel we own and publish a price for is **60 inches**, which is larger than a 55, so anything a 55 inch screen would have covered is covered by ours.

A 55 inch request is almost always a room measurement rather than a brand preference: somebody has worked out roughly how big the screen needs to be for the back row to read a slide. If that is your situation, tell us the room depth and the guest count instead of the diagonal, and we will tell you plainly whether the 60 inch panel reads from the back or whether your room has outgrown a flat panel and wants a projected image instead, covered in our [projector rental](/blog/projector-rental/) guide.

Where a flat panel genuinely cannot be swapped for projection is a bright room: see [TV Screen or Projector](#tv-screen-or-projector-which-one-does-your-event-need) above.

### Is a stand included with the screen?

Yes. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a designer stand with the 60 inch display, so it arrives ready to position rather than needing a separate mount or table.

### Can I rent multiple TV screens for one event?

Yes, but not off this page's price, and the distinction matters.

**What we own** is one 60 inch panel, the one included in the published [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) at 490 euros ex VAT. Every price and every spec above describes that single screen.

**Anything beyond one screen is a sourced job**, quoted individually rather than sold from stock. At [ECOC 2026 at FYCMA](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-supplies-display-screens-for-exhibitor-stands-at-ecoc-2026-in-malaga/) we supplied and installed the display screens across exhibitor stands throughout the hall, several stands taking more than one and one taking five in a row along a single wall. Those screens were sourced and installed for that job, not pulled from our own shelf, which is exactly why there is no published multi screen rate here. We have also put multiple TV monitors on rolling stands for a corporate project, our two day setup with [Bmotion in Marbella](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-delivers-premium-technical-support-for-bmotions-high-profile-corporate-project-in-marbella/).

[Contact us](/contact/) with your room layout, or your stand numbers, and we will scope and quote the right count.

### Is a technician needed to operate the screen?

A dedicated live AV technician is included with the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), for up to 6 continuous hours, the same technician hours inclusion that applies to the MICE Pack's sound and microphones.

### Do you rent LED video walls or modular LED panels?

Not from our own inventory. Our large format display is a single 60 inch flat panel screen, not a modular tiled video wall built from stacked LED cabinets, and LED walls and video walls, including outdoor stage scale configurations, are not part of it. See [What We Don't Stock](#what-we-dont-stock-led-video-walls-and-modular-led-panels) above.

### Is "TV screen," "display monitor" and "plasma screen" the same product?

Yes. All three terms describe the same flat panel display at Malaga Event Gear: the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s premium 60 inch high definition LED display screen. "Plasma screen" is a legacy term still used colloquially in the local market. Actual plasma display technology is not what gets installed today. See [Is a TV Screen the Same as a Display Monitor or Plasma Screen?](#is-a-tv-screen-the-same-as-a-display-monitor-or-plasma-screen) above.

### What resolution is the screen? Is it 4K?

We publish "high definition" for the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/)'s screen. We do not publish a 4K or other specific resolution figure for it, so the honest answer is high definition, not 4K.

### Can the screen be used for hybrid meetings or video conferencing?

Yes. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) is purpose built for corporate and meeting use: the screen carries the video call or presentation while the included gooseneck and wireless handheld microphones carry the room's voice to the remote side.

### Is the screen for indoor venues only, or can it go outdoors?

We do not publish an outdoor rating for this screen. The honest guidance is indoor venues, such as conference rooms, hotel ballrooms and exhibition halls. [Contact us](/contact/) with your venue details if you are considering an outdoor placement, so we can confirm what is possible rather than guess.

### How much does a TV screen rental cost?

490 euros ex VAT, for the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), which covers the 60 inch screen and stand for up to 120 guests, plus the sound system, microphones and a technician for up to 6 hours. All prices are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout. See [TV Screen Rental Pricing and What's Included](#tv-screen-rental-pricing-and-whats-included) above.
